2026-11-07T00:00:02Z (RFD66606-2475) '`tag_bench.py`, `frontier_markers.py`, and the detector variants they compare.
 # tags: rfd:scope, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2475  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:03Z (RFD66606-2475) 'Which tag family, marker size and detector settings give the fewest wrong reads at distance and tilt?
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD2475  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:04Z (RFD66606-2475) 'The first bench run was invalid: the flat sheets rendered mirrored, so flipping the frame read 263 markers instead of the expected count, which gave 3,913 of 3,917 tags "broken" and failed the control outright. That bug is fixed in `tag_bench.py`. A per-tag blocklist is not a usable gate on its own, since it only reacts to tags that already failed; the frontier table has to decide tag family, marker size and detector settings up front instead.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2475  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-2475) 'Re-render the bench and build the frontier table: detector variants crossed with distance and tilt, each cell holding its wrong-read count, plus a flipped-frame control that must itself read as broken.
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD2475  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-2475) 'Suit markers: tag bench and the marker frontier
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2475  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-2475) 'Ship the frontier table as the gate that selects tag family, marker size and detector settings, replacing any per-tag blocklist approach. Detector settings already show they matter at large marker scale: a window of 3 to 203 and a threshold constant of 3 recovered most of the unread markers at 220 px, and that setting becomes the frontier's starting point rather than a fixed default.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2475  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-2475) 'The mirrored-frame bug
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2475  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-2475) 'The flat sheets used to validate detector settings rendered mirrored left-to-right. Flipping the frame before detection recovered 263 readable markers that the un-flipped frame reported as unreadable, which inflated the broken-tag count to 3,913 of 3,917 and made the bench's own control pass for the wrong reason. `tag_bench.py` now flips consistently with the render path.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2475  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-2475) 'Frontier axes
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2475  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:11Z (RFD66606-2475) '- Tag family: which marker dictionary is painted.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2475  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:12Z (RFD66606-2475) '- Marker size: physical size in mm (and the derived pixel count at a given camera distance).
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2475  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:13Z (RFD66606-2475) '- Detector settings: adaptive-threshold window size and threshold constant.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2475  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:14Z (RFD66606-2475) '- Distance and tilt: the two viewing conditions crossed against every other axis.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2475  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:15Z (RFD66606-2475) '- Flipped-frame control: every cell also runs mirrored, and must report broken, not readable.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2475  1 LINE
 Text:Written

